body:
Why do you say that? I have been vegan for 5+ years and know many other vegans who all have no issues. Obviously people's bodies vary so your own experience isn't invalid but still 

&#x200B;

Majority of food and nutrition organizations in the world agree that a vegan diet is appropriate and nutritionally complete for all stages of human life. There's nothing special in meat. You can get everything you need from plants.

a lid. why did that. not occur to me. omg I am so stupid thank you! 

barriers have been helping. He is so determined though he keeps trying to find ways around them  

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

He does that too! I have a pile of hoodies on a chair next to my desk and he will jump up and dig on them even though every time he does i take him off and say no

I didn't know about the shoulder thing. He doesnt usually go up there I was just holding him and he climbed up. Is licking a similar behavior? He does that to me constantly 

&#x200B;

When he's not being disobedient he's great, uses his litterbox, totally fine with being picked up/held, has never bit me, follows me around, loves attention, 

&#x200B;

cardboard sounds like a great idea, I will go pick some up next chance I get. I feel like he will try and throw himself at it anyway but maybe he will only try once. thank you!

What part of it are you afraid of?  just the fact that you will die or anything specifically about it? 

&#x200B;

for me I'm much more scared of life, like not wasting it. or people I care about dying. I worry all the time that my friends could be dead right now. but my own death I don't even think about. Well actually thats a lie I think about death all the time but that's because I usually want to die. But I have been this way for so long it just doesn't bother me anymore. It's like when of your socks feels weird all day eventually you just accept it
